// Two sparks whose rings interfere where they meet.
name Twin Sparks
rule B1/S
steps 3
hint Two sparks. Where their rings would overlap, the cells had too many neighbours to be born.
tip Two sparks, six cells apart. The rings that would have touched lost their touching columns.
